  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain in place in\nvarying degrees through at least Saturday. Hot weather will\ncontinue into the weekend with highs in the 90s most of the time\nwith some locations near 100 at times. With heat impact being\nmoderate in most areas today, will not issue any heat related\nheadlines for now. \n\nSatellite showcases a large smoke plume stretched from eastern \nOregon across northern Montana. Smoke will continue to be over \nthe area today and tonight with unhealthy air quality and \nvariable visibility. \n\nWeak waves will move through the ridge at various times through \nThursday to bring chances for showers and thunderstorms to parts \nof the region. Models are showing increased instability and higher\ndew points Wednesday afternoon and evening with a cool front \nmoving through that could lead to a few severe thunderstorms. Spc \nhas upgraded to a slight risk mainly east of the Yellowstone River\nfor Wednesday with a threat of large hail and damaging winds.\n\nHigh on Thursday will be a few degrees lower before the ridge\nstrengthen Friday and Saturday. At this point, Saturday looks like\nit will be very hot with highs above 100 in most areas. \n\nRidge moves east Saturday night and upper trough moves for Sunday\nand Monday. A strong dry cold front on Sunday is expected to bring\ngusty NW winds followed by much cooler temperatures on Monday.  \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather continuing through Saturday. \nLow confidence in timing any showers and thunderstorms.\n\nNBM Deviations include HRRR/RAP blends to enhance visibility \nreductions due to smoke and tweaking pops at times today and\ntonight to account for weak waves moving through the area.",
